msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The purpose of analysing factorial and response surface designs is to "
"identify influential factors and optimal response conditions. The analysis "
"shows which factors significantly affect the response and how they interact. "
"This allows to systematically optimize processes and improve product quality."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Analysis of variance table"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The analysis of variance (ANOVA) table splits the variation in the response "
"into the parts explained by the terms of the model and the part the model "
"does not explain (Error)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Columns"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Sum of squares"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Variation in the response attributed to the source."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Degrees of freedom. For a term, the number of model coefficients it contains "
"(fewer when some of its contrasts are aliased)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Mean square"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Sum of squares divided by df."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Mean square of the source divided by the mean square of Error."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Probability of an F-value at least this large if all coefficients of the "
"source are zero."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Rows"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Tests whether the model explains any variation, i.e. whether at least one "
"coefficient besides the intercept differs from zero. Its sum of squares "
"equals Total minus Error and is the same for all sums of squares types."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Linear terms, Squared terms, Interaction terms, Covariates"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Joint test of all terms in the group, e.g. whether all linear effects are "
"zero. The group is treated as one term and adjusted according to the "
"selected sums of squares type."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Single terms"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Test of one term (listed below its group), adjusted according to the "
"selected sums of squares type."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Block"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Test of the differences between blocks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Error"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Variation the model does not explain. Its mean square estimates the noise "
"variance and is the denominator of all F-tests."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Lack of fit, Pure error"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Shown below Error when the design has replicated runs, e.g. center points. "
"Pure error is the variation between replicates. Lack of fit tests whether "
"the model misses systematic variation such as curvature; a small p-value "
"indicates a poor fit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Total"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Total variation of the response around its mean, with df equal to the number "
"of runs minus 1. Model plus Error equals Total."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"With type I sums of squares, and in balanced (orthogonal) designs, the term "
"rows add up to their group row, and the group rows and Block add up to "
"Model. With type II or III sums of squares in unbalanced designs this is "
"generally not the case: when terms are correlated, part of the variation can "
"be explained by several terms, and this shared part is not attributed to any "
"single term."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "References"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "R Packages"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Select the type of experimental design you want to analyse."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"A factorial design is an experimental setup used to study the effects of "
"multiple factors by varying them simultaneously. Each factor is tested at "
"different levels and in different combinations with other factors. This "
"design allows for the examination of both the main effects of each factor "
"and the interactions between factors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"A response surface design is an experimental framework used to optimize and "
"understand the relationships between several explanatory variables and one "
"or more response variables. Besides main effects and interactions, it allows "
"to estimate squared terms, which describe the curvature of the response. "
"This gives a detailed map of the response landscape, which helps to find "
"optimal conditions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The measured outcome variables of the process under investigation. Each "
"response is analysed separately."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "The columns corresponding to the discrete factors in the design."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "The columns corresponding to the continuous factors in the design."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The columns corresponding to the covariates in the design. The difference "
"between a covariate and a continuous factor is that the covariate will not "
"be analysed for interaction effects and is excluded from effect plots."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The column corresponding to the blocks in the design. The difference between "
"a block variable and a discrete factor is that the blocks will not be "
"analysed for interaction effects and are excluded from effect plots."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"For the ordering of contrasts and to identify the alpha points in a response "
"surface design, the low and high levels of all factors need to be specified. "
"There are two options to handle this."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Attempts to automatically detect the low and high levels by taking the "
"minimum and maximum for continuous factors, and by ordering discrete factors "
"alphabetically. For response surface designs, this might recognize alpha "
"values as low/high levels. In this case, manual specification is needed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Shows all factors in the analysis to allow for manual specification of the "
"low and high levels."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Enter the low and high level of each factor. Blocks and discrete factors "
"with more than two levels are not rescaled to -1/1, so they have no low and "
"high level (\"Not available\")."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Not available"
msgstr ""

