msgid "Assign alias names to the factors. Useful when factors have long names."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the regression coefficients as an equation predicting the response."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the results in coded units. This means that the levels of continuous "
"factors and of discrete factors with two levels are rescaled to lie between "
"-1 and 1. Discrete factors with more than two levels are not rescaled: a "
"factor with k levels enters the model with k-1 terms (sum-to-zero "
"contrasts), as in uncoded units, and their low/high levels are not used. For "
"factorial designs, the ANOVA table is calculated in coded units, so it does "
"not change with this option, unless coding changes the model (an interaction "
"or squared term without its main effects)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Confidence intervals"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Add confidence intervals for the effects and the coefficients to the "
"coefficients table, based on the t-distribution with the error degrees of "
"freedom. The interval for an effect is twice the interval for its "
"coefficient (in coded units)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Confidence level of the intervals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
